<title>DENMARK: Danish October unemployment falls to 8.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish October unemployment falls to 8.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's seasonally adjusted unemployment was 8.3 percent of the workforce in October, down from 8.4 percent in September, the National Statistics Office said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>				Oct 1996    Sept 1996   Oct 1995</p>
<p>    Unemployment rate    8.3 pct	8.4 pct     9.7 pct</p>
<p>    Total unemployed     233,100	235,200    272,100</p>
<p>All above figures seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>NOTE - A panel of economists polled by Reuters had on average forecast October unemployment of 8.3 percent.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650.</p>
</text>
